+## Also (0.4.0, native menu state, window options, open paths)
+
+- Menu entries: `MenuEntry::Check` (tick) and `MenuEntry::Submenu` (up to 4 levels); ids must be unique. Set state at runtime with `rk_shell_set_menu_item_enabled`, `rk_shell_set_menu_item_checked` or the batch `rk_shell_set_menu_state`. Clicks on every item id, custom ones included, arrive as `rightkit-shell://menu`.
+- Menu layout (HIG order App, File, Edit, View, app groups, Window, Help; defaults unchanged): `MenuSpec.file` adds/extends File; `edit_extra` appends entries (e.g. a Find submenu) to Edit; `view_entries` / `view_fullscreen` shape View; `window_entries` / `window_compact` shape Window; `omit_empty_help` skips an empty Help; `app_compact` drops About and Services from the macOS app menu; `overrides: [MenuOverride{role: undo|redo|quit|close-window, id}]` swaps a native item for an app-id item that keeps the native label and accelerator and emits `rightkit-shell://menu` (app items have no responder-chain enablement; drive it with `rk_shell_set_menu_state`); an app overriding Undo/Redo owns their enablement and, when focus is in a plain text input, must forward to the webview's native undo/redo (e.g. `document.execCommand('undo')`) so a search box's undo isn't stolen. `menu::plan` computes the layout without native objects.
+- File associations (`associations`, Orthic-Labs/rightkit#670): the app passes `AssociationSpec { bundle_id, groups: [{ id, extensions, utis, windows_prog_id }] }` per call. `associations::status` reports, per group and per target (UTI on macOS, `extension:.ext` on Windows), who the default handler is and whether it is the app; `associations::set_defaults` makes the running app the default on macOS (NSWorkspace `setDefaultApplicationAtURL:toOpenContentType:completionHandler:` on the main thread so the consent sheet can show, one shared timeout, `LSSetDefaultRoleHandlerForContentType` only if that selector is absent, result re-read) and on Windows opens Settings > Default apps and returns `user_action_required` (`UserChoice` is hash-protected and never written; status reads UserChoice, then HKCU/HKCR class default, and compares the ProgID case-insensitively). `associations::open_default_apps` uses `os_settings`. Commands `rk_shell_associations_status`, `rk_shell_associations_set`, `rk_shell_open_default_apps`; JS `shell.associations`.
+- `WindowSpec`: `parent`, `visible: false` (created hidden, you show it), `resizable`, `shadow`. `rk_shell_window` also takes `resize`, `center`, `set-resizable`, `set-maximizable` and `destroy`.
+- File open: argv paths from the first launch and from second launches queue until the renderer calls `rk_shell_open_paths_ready`; later ones are emitted as `rightkit-shell://open-paths`. Route each path through the broker before reading it.
+- Engine stream and policy (0.4.0): `rk_shell_engine_subscribe` is a snapshot-atomic stream over a Tauri Channel (receiver first, then the allowlisted snapshot method); `EnginePolicy::stream_coalesce` coalesces progress by key. Renderer: `shell.engine.subscribe`, `callTagged`, `status`.
+- Surfaces, dialogs, drag-drop: `ShellBuilder::surface("legal", 960.0, 640.0)` + `shell.surface.set("legal")` sizes, centres and shows the calling window through the reveal guard. With the `dialog` feature `shell.dialog.pickFiles / pickFolder / save` return broker-granted paths (the app also registers `tauri_plugin_dialog::init()`). `ShellBuilder::drop_events(true)` emits `rightkit-shell://drop` with granted paths. `shell.window.setFullscreen(bool)` is explicit.
+- Settings, models and secrets without a sidecar: `ShellBuilder::host_handlers(HostHandlers::new().settings(AppSettingsHost::new(store)).secrets(CredentialsHost::new(creds)).models(my_models))` answers `rightkit.settings.*`, `rightkit.models.*` and `rightkit.secrets.*` (the `@rightkit/settings-ui` `createShellBackends` contract) in-process; adapters need the `host-app-settings` / `host-credentials` features. `shell.settings.importLocalStorage({ keys, remove })` is the one-time move of old `localStorage` preferences.
+- Windows start-up: `ShellBuilder::sync_window_icon(true)` fixes the taskbar and Alt+Tab icon (`WM_SETICON`); `startup_error::show_and_exit("MyApp", &err)` reports a fatal start-up error in a native dialog; `webview2_env::configure` sets the WebView2 user-data folder.
+- Close and recreate: `close_behavior(CloseBehavior::DestroyAndRecreate)` + `on_recreate(|app, source| ...)` destroys the main window on close and builds it again when the shell would reveal it. `pickers::pick_folder` / `pick_app` are plain-Rust native pickers. `consent` is the native Deny / Allow once / Always allow dialog with per-origin grants (`GrantStore`); `ShellBuilder::pinned_origin` pins the origin popups and grants are judged against.
+- Non-Tauri apps (Pulse, a CLI, a daemon): `rightkit-tauri-shell = { version = "0.4", default-features = false, features = ["wv2-0_38"] }` gives `clipboard::read` / `write` / `take_item`, `autostart`, `SingleInstance::claim`, `pickers`, `consent`, `notify` and `ShellError` without compiling Tauri. The Tauri-only modules are not there.
+- DevTools keys: `devtools::set_inspector_shortcut_scope` is Rust-only, off by default, and refuses to enable in a build without `content-devtools` or `dev-inspect` (settled decision rightkit#771 D2: ViewRight is the only app that may enable it).
+
