+// Everything that needs Tauri (the plugin, the builder, the managed state, the commands and the
+// modules above that are gated on `feature = "tauri"`) lives in `shell.rs`, pasted in here so its
+// items keep their crate-root paths and privacy. With `default-features = false` (and a `wv2-*`
+// feature on Windows) the crate is the Tauri-free core: errors, path broker, rich clipboard,
+// autostart and login items, single instance, notifications, presence, recovery, consent,
+// pickers and the settings / models / secrets host handlers, with no `tauri` dependency.
