 # Changelog
 
+## 0.2.0
+
+Additive; needs `rightkit-tauri-shell` 0.4.0 for the new calls (an older host rejects them with "Command ... not found").
+
+- `MenuEntry` gains `{ kind: 'check' }` and `{ kind: 'submenu' }`. `menu.setChecked(id, checked)` and `menu.setState([{ id, enabled?, checked? }])` change native item state by id; `menu.onClick` already receives custom ids. New type `MenuItemState`.
+- `window.resize(w, h)`, `window.center()`, `window.setResizable(b)`, `window.setMaximizable(b)`, `window.destroy()`.
+- `WindowSpec` gains `parent`, `visible`, `resizable`, `shadow` (and types the existing `minWidth`, `minHeight`, `decorations`, `center`, `fullscreen`, `skipTaskbar`, `x`, `y`).
+- `openPaths.ready()` returns the queued launch and second-launch file paths and starts live delivery; `openPaths.on(handler)` receives later ones. `EVENTS.openPaths`.
+- `associations.status(spec, groupIds?)`, `associations.set(spec, groupIds?, timeoutMs?)` and `associations.openDefaultApps()` over `rk_shell_associations_status`, `rk_shell_associations_set` and `rk_shell_open_default_apps`. Types `AssociationSpec`, `AssociationGroup`, `AssociationStatus`, `AssociationGroupStatus`, `AssociationHandlerStatus`, `AssociationSetResult`.
+- Engine: `engine.callTagged(method, params?, tag?)` (structured `{code, message, origin}` errors), `engine.status()`, and `engine.subscribe(handler, { snapshotMethod?, params?, tag? })`, a snapshot-atomic stream over a Tauri Channel that returns `{ snapshot, lifecycle, close }`. `EngineEvent` gains optional `id` and `tag`; new types `EngineCallError`, `EngineLifecycle`, `TaggedEngineEvent`, `EngineSubscription`, `EngineSubscribeOptions`. `ShellTransport` gains an optional `channel`, which `tauriTransport()` provides. `tray.onEvent` payloads carry an optional `trayId`.
+- `engine.call` for `rightkit.settings.*`, `rightkit.models.*` and `rightkit.secrets.*` (answered by the host's in-process handlers) rejects with `{ code, message, origin: 'host' }` instead of the plain `"code: message"` string, so `@rightkit/settings-ui` sees `revision_conflict`. Other methods keep the string. New `HostCallError` type.
+- `settings.importLocalStorage({ keys, storage?, remove?, overwrite? })`: one-time move of `localStorage` preferences into the host settings document (a key the host already has wins unless `overwrite`).
+- `window.setFullscreen(bool)`, `surface.set(name)`, `dialog.pickFiles / pickFolder / save` (host feature `dialog`), `drop.on(handler)` with `EVENTS.drop` and `DropEvent`, for the host's `drop_events(true)`.
+- Tests: new cases in `tests/shell.test.mjs`.
+
 ## Unreleased
 
 - Renamed from @rightkit/shell; @rightkit/shell@0.1.1 remains published under the old name.
