 `rk_shell_capabilities` is read-only and returns `{ quitDrain: bool, notifyBypassDnd: bool }`. The `rightkit-tauri-shell` crate implements both; it always reports `notifyBypassDnd: true` and reports `quitDrain: true` only when the app opts in. On a host without the support, the capability-gated calls reject with `unsupported`.
 
+## Menu state, window actions, open paths (0.2.0)
+
+Needs `rightkit-tauri-shell` 0.4.0.
+
+```ts
+await shell.menu.setState([{ id: 'vr-cmd:bold', enabled: true }, { id: 'vr-cmd:view-wrap', checked: true }]);
+await shell.window.resize(480, 560); await shell.window.center();
+await shell.window.open({ label: 'print-preview', parent: 'main', visible: false, resizable: true, shadow: true });
+const off = await shell.openPaths.on((paths) => openFiles(paths));
+openFiles(await shell.openPaths.ready()); // register `on` first
+```
+
+## Engine stream, host settings, dialogs, surfaces, drag-drop (0.2.0)
+
+```ts
+const shell = createShell();
+// Snapshot-atomic stream: events that arrive while the snapshot runs are not lost.
+const sub = await shell.engine.subscribe((frame) => render(frame), { snapshotMethod: 'jobs.list' });
+sub.snapshot; sub.lifecycle; sub.close();
+
+// Host-answered preferences (Rust: ShellBuilder::host_handlers). createShellBackends(shell) from
+// @rightkit/settings-ui/shell-adapter works unchanged; rejections carry { code: 'revision_conflict' }.
+await shell.settings.importLocalStorage({ keys: ['theme', 'sidebar'], remove: true });
+
+await shell.surface.set('legal');            // host: ShellBuilder::surface("legal", 960, 640)
+await shell.window.setFullscreen(true);
+const files = await shell.dialog.pickFiles({ multiple: true, filters: [{ name: 'Images', extensions: ['png'] }] });
+const off = await shell.drop.on((e) => { if (e.phase === 'drop') use(e.paths); }); // host: drop_events(true)
+```
+
+`engine.subscribe` needs a transport with a `channel` (the default `tauriTransport()` has one; a custom test transport rejects with `unsupported`). `dialog.*` needs the Rust crate's `dialog` feature.
+
